A municipal election can be set aside if the Prescribed Authority finds, among other grounds, that:
• the elected candidate was not qualified or was disqualified on the election date;
• corrupt practice was committed by the candidate, their agent, or another person with the candidate’s consent;
• a nomination paper was wrongly rejected;
• the result was affected by wrongly accepting a nomination, corrupt practice, or wrongly receiving/refusing/rejecting votes. 
This is under the Bihar Municipal Act, 2007, section 479. This is general information, not legal advice. [
